#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The North German Plain: Lower Saxony, November 1983.  A sample game
for the Grognard engine, and a war that never happened.

The same war as the Fulda Gap, two hundred kilometres to the north: the
3rd Shock Army attacks the British I Corps on the open country between
the inner-German border and the Weser, and the British must come
forward from their barracks to meet it while the Royal Engineers blow
the bridges behind the covering force.  Play either side against the
computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./northag (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.northag.json.  ./northag --selftest checks the map and plays
a game between two computer players.
"""

